__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
CAPABILITIES.md
# Transient run outputs: eval-report.json, lint-report.json and friends are regenerated by every
# `make eval` / lint invocation and say nothing that the command's own exit code does not.
*-report.json
# ...but a CRITIC report is not transient. It costs real money to produce (the six committed ones
# are 1002 judged calls, ~$123-equivalent), eval replays it as the entire soft_critic tier, and it
# is stamped with the digest of the IR it judged so a stale one is detected rather than trusted.
# spec-01's copy survived the glob above only because it happens to be called `critic-report.FULL
# .json`; the five added on 2026-08-27 are named for their siblings (`document-ir.yaml`), match the
# glob exactly, and would have been dropped in silence. Un-ignoring them is the point, not a
# convenience: an ignored critic report is a silent skip with a receipt.
!skills/deep-primer/tests/fixtures/**/critic-report.json
run-manifest.json
.DS_Store
.specstory/
.claude/

# Fetched source bodies from grounding campaigns. The campaign METADATA (ledger, leads, briefs,
# concept maps, campaign-run.json) is committed so provenance stays auditable; the corpus itself is
# whole third-party pages we retrieved, and redistributing them is exactly what the ≤15-word quote
# rule exists to avoid. Re-fetchable from the urls in source-ledger.yaml.
skills/deep-primer/tests/fixtures/*-grounded/corpus/
